Robin Lee Powell scripsit:

> On the other hand, the grammar says that "mi .eparoibo do broda" should
> parse.

Aaaah, at last one I understand and can fix.  The big switch statement
starting at line 168 of lexruleo.c is a guard which prevents the complex
and heavily backtracking tense grammar from being started if the first
word can't possibly be part of a tense.  Unfortunately, PA_672 is not
in this list, so if a simple_tag starts with PA, it won't be parsed.
So just add after line 168 the line "PA_672:" and recompile.  Don't re-run
yacc, or Ghu only knows what will happen.

